course: dictionary
lesson: 8126
title: Repent: feeling sorry and changing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To repent means to feel truly sorry for something wrong you have done, and to want to change. Saying sorry is not always enough: repenting means you really mean it and you try to do better.
explain: Read the context. «Jonah preached, the whole city of Nineveh repented, and God spared it.» The people felt sorry for their wrongs and changed, and the sentence tells you what happened next. Ask yourself what would fit in place of repented: "felt sorry and changed" makes sense.
explain: «Christians believe that God forgives people who truly repent, even after great wrongs.» The word truly is a clue. Repenting is not pretend sorrow; it is real sorrow that leads to change. Swap in "feel sorry and change" to check the meaning still fits.
explain: Repent can also be formal, meaning to regret a choice: «He repented of his decision.» Here you can be sorry about a choice, not only about a sin. The old saying «marry in haste, repent at leisure» means you may be sorry later, once you have had time to think.
fact: Repent is a verb: repent, repents, repented, repenting.
fact: «Repent» means to feel truly sorry for a wrong and want to change.
fact: In church and Bible use, to repent means to turn away from sin and turn back to God.
fact: «Repent of your sins» and «repent and be forgiven» are common phrases.
fact: Repentance is a key idea in Christianity, Judaism and Islam: saying sorry to God and to the person you hurt, and then changing.
exercise: «The whole city of Nineveh repented.» What does repented mean here? | *Felt truly sorry and changed their ways | Ran away from the city | Built a big new wall | Forgot all about the matter
exercise: Which word means to feel truly sorry for a wrong and want to change? | *repent | respect | reheat | repeat
exercise: «He repented of his decision.» What does repented mean in this sentence? | Forgot his decision | Made the same choice again | *Regretted the choice he made | Cheered loudly for his choice
test: What does «repent at leisure» mean? | Being happy about a choice straight away | Doing the same thing again and again | Being angry at someone else | *Being sorry later, once there is time to think
test: «Christians believe that God forgives people who truly repent.» Why does the word truly matter? | It means the same as sorry, so it is not needed | It is there to make the sentence longer | *It shows that real sorrow and change are needed | It shows that pretend sorrow is enough
exam: Which sentence shows someone who repents? | *He said sorry to his sister and promised to change his ways | He ate the whole cake and went out to play | The dog ran into the garden | She laughed and did the same wrong again
